// LLAMP-SPEC v1 | ADR-037
=adr: 037
=title: Workspace/Derived Variable Convention — ADR-031 Namespace Implementation
=date: 2026-02-27
=status: accepted implements=ADR-031(namespace_semantics) supersedes=trigger.stateData.*

#ctx
~problem: ADR-031 defined workspace.*/derived.* namespaces but code used trigger.stateData.* (read)
  and plain attr names (write). Inconsistency; no support for nested telemetry paths.
~requirement: implement ADR-031 namespace_semantics as clean break

#decision
=workspace: top-level context variable = device_states.data.* (the triggering doc's raw telemetry)
  → {{workspace.freq}} resolves telemetry field 'freq'
  → {{workspace.meter_Params.frequence}} resolves nested telemetry path
=derived: mapping key prefix in writeDeviceState node
  → key column accepts {{derived.attr}} syntax
  → backend parses attr from {{derived.attr}}, validates against device.attributes
  → plain key fallback still works for backwards compat
=trigger.stateData: REMOVED (clean break — seed script and existing workflows updated)
=workspace_at_root: engine adds workspace to root context at init + after trigger fires
  → resolves from inputData.workspace at init; reseeds from context.trigger.workspace post-trigger

#impl
=dispatcher: data.workspace = stateData.data; data.timestamp = stateData.timestamp (no stateData key)
=engine: context.workspace seeded from inputData.workspace at init + after trigger node fires
=handlers: extractDerive(key) parses {{derived.attr}} → attr; fallback to plain key
=seed_script: context.trigger.stateData.* → context.workspace.*; mapping keys → {{derived.attr}}
=ui_panel: column headers renamed Output(derived.*)/Input(workspace.*); datalist → {{derived.attr}}
=variable_picker: workspace.attr suggestions; section header "Workspace Variables"
=workflow_variables: getDeviceAttributeVariables keys → workspace.${fieldName}

#consequences
+pos: [matches_ADR-031_semantics, nested_telemetry_supported, explicit_read/write_distinction]
-neg: [breaking_change_requires_seed_and_existing_workflow_updates]
